---
import Layout from '../../../components/Layout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Layout title="What is Lo Shu Grid? - Numero Girija">
    <div class="breadcrumb">
        <a href={`${base}learn/`}>Learning Portal</a> / <a href={`${base}learn/basics/`}>Grid Basics</a> / What is Lo Shu Grid?
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h1 class="section-title">📖 What is Lo Shu Grid?</h1>

        <div class="content-section">
            <h2>The Ancient Magic Square</h2>
            <p>
                The Lo Shu Grid, also known as the Lo Shu Square or Magic Square of Saturn, is an ancient Chinese mathematical diagram that dates back over 4,000 years. It is a 3×3 grid where numbers 1-9 are arranged in such a way that each row, column, and diagonal adds up to 15 — the number of days in each of the 24 cycles of the Chinese solar year.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="grid-example">
            <div class="magic-square">
                <div class="cell">4</div>
                <div class="cell">9</div>
                <div class="cell">2</div>
                <div class="cell">3</div>
                <div class="cell">5</div>
                <div class="cell">7</div>
                <div class="cell">8</div>
                <div class="cell">1</div>
                <div class="cell">6</div>
            </div>
            <p class="caption">The Traditional Lo Shu Square: Every row, column, and diagonal sums to 15</p>
        </div>

        <div class="content-section">
            <h2>🐢 The Legend</h2>
            <p>
                According to Chinese mythology, the Lo Shu pattern was first revealed to humans around 2800 BCE during the reign of Emperor Yu the Great. A turtle emerged from the Yellow River (Lo River) with peculiar markings on its shell. The markings formed a 3×3 grid pattern with dots representing numbers 1 through 9. This divine pattern became known as "Lo Shu," meaning "Luo River Writing."
            </p>
            <p>
                The ancient Chinese considered this pattern sacred and magical because of its perfect mathematical balance. It became a fundamental element in Feng Shui, I Ching divination, and eventually numerology.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="content-section">
            <h2>🔢 From Magic Square to Personal Grid</h2>
            <p>
                In modern numerology, the Lo Shu Grid is adapted to create personal charts based on an individual's date of birth. Rather than the traditional arrangement, numbers from your birth date are plotted onto the 3×3 grid according to their positions. This creates a unique energetic blueprint that reveals:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>Your personality traits and natural talents</li>
                <li>Missing numbers indicating areas of challenge or growth</li>
                <li>Repetitive numbers showing amplified energies</li>
                <li>Planes and arrows revealing thinking patterns</li>
                <li>Life path and destiny indicators</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="content-section">
            <h2>🌟 Grid Structure & Positions</h2>
            <p>
                The Lo Shu Grid is divided into 9 positions, each with specific meanings:
            </p>
            <div class="positions-grid">
                <div class="position">
                    <div class="pos-num">4</div>
                    <div class="pos-label">Mind & Logic</div>
                </div>
                <div class="position">
                    <div class="pos-num">9</div>
                    <div class="pos-label">Spirituality</div>
                </div>
                <div class="position">
                    <div class="pos-num">2</div>
                    <div class="pos-label">Emotions</div>
                </div>
                <div class="position">
                    <div class="pos-num">3</div>
                    <div class="pos-label">Creativity</div>
                </div>
                <div class="position">
                    <div class="pos-num">5</div>
                    <div class="pos-label">Balance</div>
                </div>
                <div class="position">
                    <div class="pos-num">7</div>
                    <div class="pos-label">Intuition</div>
                </div>
                <div class="position">
                    <div class="pos-num">8</div>
                    <div class="pos-label">Action</div>
                </div>
                <div class="position">
                    <div class="pos-num">1</div>
                    <div class="pos-label">Communication</div>
                </div>
                <div class="position">
                    <div class="pos-num">6</div>
                    <div class="pos-label">Materialism</div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="content-section">
            <h2>✨ Why Use Lo Shu Grid?</h2>
            <p>
                The Lo Shu Grid provides a visual, mathematical approach to understanding your life's energetic patterns. Unlike other numerology systems that focus solely on calculations, the Lo Shu Grid offers:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Visual Clarity:</strong> See your energetic strengths and weaknesses at a glance</li>
                <li><strong>Holistic View:</strong> Understand the interplay between different aspects of your personality</li>
                <li><strong>Practical Insights:</strong> Identify specific areas for personal development</li>
                <li><strong>Ancient Wisdom:</strong> Based on thousands of years of Chinese metaphysical knowledge</li>
                <li><strong>Actionable Remedies:</strong> Clear guidance on how to balance missing energies</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="next-steps">
            <h3>Ready to Learn More?</h3>
            <div class="next-links">
                <a href={`${base}learn/basics/making-grid/`} class="next-link">
                    <span>Next: How to Make Your Grid →</span>
                </a>
                <a href={`${base}learn/basics/understanding-grid/`} class="next-link">
                    <span>Reading Grid Positions →</span>
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <style>
        .breadcrumb {
            color: #666;
            font-size: 0.85rem;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
            font-weight: 500;
        }

        .breadcrumb a {
            color: #6b3fa0;
            text-decoration: none;
        }

        .breadcrumb a:hover {
            text-decoration: underline;
        }

        .content-section {
            margin-bottom: 30px;
        }

        .content-section h2 {
            color: #2d1b69;
            font-size: 1.3rem;
            font-weight: 800;
            margin-bottom: 16px;
            margin-top: 24px;
        }

        .content-section p {
            color: #444;
            font-size: 0.95rem;
            line-height: 1.8;
            margin-bottom: 16px;
        }

        .content-section ul {
            color: #444;
            font-size: 0.95rem;
            line-height: 1.8;
            margin-left: 20px;
            margin-bottom: 16px;
        }

        .content-section li {
            margin-bottom: 10px;
        }

        .grid-example {
            background: linear-gradient(135deg, #f9f5ff, #f0ebff);
            padding: 30px;
            border-radius: 16px;
            margin: 30px 0;
            text-align: center;
        }

        .magic-square {
            display: inline-grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
            gap: 3px;
            background: #6b3fa0;
            padding: 3px;
            border-radius: 12px;
            margin-bottom: 16px;
        }

        .magic-square .cell {
            background: white;
            width: 70px;
            height: 70px;
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            font-size: 2rem;
            font-weight: 900;
            color: #2d1b69;
        }

        .caption {
            color: #6b3fa0;
            font-size: 0.85rem;
            font-weight: 600;
        }

        .positions-grid {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
            gap: 12px;
            margin: 20px 0;
        }

        .position {
            background: #fafafa;
            border: 2px solid #e8e8e8;
            border-radius: 12px;
            padding: 16px;
            text-align: center;
        }

        .pos-num {
            font-size: 2rem;
            font-weight: 900;
            color: #6b3fa0;
            margin-bottom: 8px;
        }

        .pos-label {
            font-size: 0.8rem;
            color: #666;
            font-weight: 600;
        }

        .next-steps {
            background: linear-gradient(135deg, #fff9e5, #ffedd5);
            border: 2px solid #f59e0b;
            border-radius: 16px;
            padding: 24px;
            margin-top: 40px;
        }

        .next-steps h3 {
            color: #f59e0b;
            font-size: 1.1rem;
            font-weight: 800;
            margin-bottom: 16px;
        }

        .next-links {
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            gap: 12px;
        }

        .next-link {
            background: white;
            border: 2px solid #f59e0b;
            border-radius: 10px;
            padding: 14px 18px;
            text-decoration: none;
            color: #f59e0b;
            font-weight: 700;
            font-size: 0.9rem;
            transition: all 0.2s;
            text-align: center;
        }

        .next-link:hover {
            background: #f59e0b;
            color: white;
            transform: translateX(4px);
        }

        @media (min-width: 480px) {
            .magic-square .cell {
                width: 90px;
                height: 90px;
                font-size: 2.5rem;
            }
        }

        @media (min-width: 768px) {
            .next-links {
                flex-direction: row;
            }
        }
    </style>
</Layout>
